			<summary>Layer Seven</summary>
			<p>The seventh layer, also known as the Application or End User Layer, is the top layer of the OSI model. It helps programs like web browsers or email apps use the network to send and receive data.
				<details>	
					<summary>Protocol Examples</summary>
						<ol>
						<li>HTTP(Hyper Text Transfer Protocol) was used as the foundation for the World Wide Web. We now use HTTPS(Hyper Text Transfer Protocol Secure) because it is more secure.</li>
						<li>FTP(File Transfer Protocol) was used to transfer files from one device to another. We now use SFTP(Secure File Transfer Protocol) because it is more secure.</li>
						<li>IRC(Internet Relay Chat) was used as an online chat room for people to interact online. We now use programs like Discord or Slack, which provide a safer chat room expierence.</li>
						<li>SSH(Secure Shell) is used to create encrypted connections to a computer, enabling a secure login between those two computers.</li> 
						<li>DNS(Domain Name System) is used to narrow down questions asked in a prompt to attempt to answer a question.</li> 
						</ol>
				</details>
			</p>
			
		</details>	
